Comment (internal/service/notificationtroubleshooting/service.go:736):
**🔴 BUG-API-1: `missing_destination` warnings fire for user-fanout-only notification types.**

During e2e testing the Health tab showed `missing_destination` warnings for `TASK_AVAILABLE`, `TASK_DAILY_DIGEST`, `RISK_NOTIFICATIONS`, and `WORKFLOW_EXECUTION_FAILED`. These are user-fanout types — they don't use system destinations at all, so the warning is a false positive.

The guard here (`supportsSystemDestination(name)`) delegates to `notification.NormalizeSystemNotificationName`, which appears to return `ok=true` for those types because they are valid normalized notification names, not because they support system destinations.

**Fix:** `supportsSystemDestination` must be narrowed to only return `true` for notification types that actually accept a configured system destination. Based on the current destination model that is only `EVIDENCE_DIGEST` (and `WORKFLOW_EXECUTION_FAILED` if that is intentional — please clarify). All user-fanout types (`TASK_AVAILABLE`, `TASK_DAILY_DIGEST`, `RISK_NOTIFICATIONS`, `POAM_*`) must return `false`.

Example:
```go
func supportsSystemDestination(name string) bool {
    switch strings.ToLower(name) {
    case notification.SystemNotificationNameEvidenceDigest:
        return true
    default:
        return false
    }
}
```
